      "title": "Head Coach, Premier Club Sports (STUNT)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Head Coach, Premier Club Sports  Department: Intercollegiate Athletics Reports to: Premier Club Sport Director Appointment: Part-time; 20 hours per week (12-month position) Status: Exempt Job Summary : Bradley recently launched a Premier Club Sports division, offering an exciting opportunity for passionate and driven individuals to help build and elevate the   club sport of STUNT (AKA - Women’s Competitive Cheer) to competitive success within the sport league or conference. Working collaboratively with club leadership and the Premier Club Sport Director, the Head Coach will provide leadership, mentorship, and day-to-day management of the team while enhancing the student’s overall college experience.  Qualifications : Bachelor's degree required. Proven ability to work effectively with students and campus partners to support recruiting and program development. Experience with fundraising and program advancement efforts. Available to work evenings and weekends. (Most games occur Friday and Saturday). Demonstrated experience working with college-age students. (Preferred) Must hold or be willing to obtain required coaching certifications in accordance with league and university compliance standards. Strong leadership, communication, and motivational skills with a commitment to fostering a positive, inclusive, and competitive team culture.   Benefits : This is a part-time, stipend position CPR and AED certification will be provided and required. Responsibilities : This position reports directly to Premier Club Sport Director. Sufficient time will be given to the following: Develop and implement effective practice plans, game strategies, and overall team management approaches to enhance team performance. Focus on player development by providing individual and group instruction to improve skills, conditioning, and game awareness. Assist in identifying and recruiting talented athletes; attend competitive events and evaluate prospective student-athletes in collaboration with the Enrollment Management - (Essential). Manage the team during competition, making real-time strategic decisions and ensuring clear communication among athletes. Promote athlete safety, support injury prevention and management, and foster student development, teamwork, and sportsmanship. Oversee logistical operations including scheduling, travel, equipment management, budgeting, and compliance with university and league regulations, in coordination with the Premier Club Sport Director. Represent the program at community and university events, fostering positive public relations and building visibility and support for the team Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:   https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
