      "title": "Police Dispatcher",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-06-01\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Police Dispatcher Department: University Police Reports to: Shift Commander, Patrol Division Appointment: Days and hours to be determined  Pay rate: $23.25 per hour (Once 60 calendar day probation is completed, pay rate increases to $23.50 per hour) **Applications submitted without a resume and cover letter will not be considered** Summary: Reporting to the Captain of the Patrol Division, the Police Dispatcher is a non-sworn support staff team member responsible for maintaining public safety communications. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide public safety communications for university police and other university departments as well as surrounding agencies. Use computer-aided dispatch system, receive and respond to routine and emergency calls requesting police, escort services, fire, medical, other emergency services, or non- emergency services. Determine the nature and location of the request or emergency; determine priorities, and dispatch police, fire, ambulance, other emergency units, or other non-emergency units as necessary and in accordance with established procedures. Receive and process emergency calls, maintain contact with all units on assignment, maintain status and location of police and fire units and coordinate response to incidents. Monitor alarms as well as security and surveillance cameras to deter, detect and report criminal activities. Answer non-emergency calls for assistance. Provide direction to campus visitors and assist walk-in victims of crime or individuals expressing specific safety and security concerns. Enter, update and retrieve information from a variety of computer systems. Receive requests for information regarding parking, vehicle registration, driving records and warrants, and provides pertinent data. Monitor several complex public safety radio frequencies. Operate a variety of communications equipment, including but not limited to, radio consoles, telephones and computer systems. Type letters, forms, and reports and maintain accurate, up-to-date files and logs. Maintain current knowledge of: FCC regulations for telecommunications, policies, procedures and practices of emergency communications and dispatch operations and basic law enforcement, fire, hazmat and EMS procedures. Process inventory. Performs duties outlined under Work Control (including but not limited to: operate University telephone system; answer incoming phone calls; forward calls to appropriate individual or office; coordinate the input to computer work orders for serviced received by the Facilities Management Department; maintain directory listing and telephone numbers for all University students, employees, offices and services) Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High school degree/completion or equivalent; Experience as receptionist, secretary, or customer service representative; flexible; dependable; skill with large volume telephone clients; skill in verbal, written and interpersonal communications; ability to respond to emergencies; adept in assigning priorities under simultaneous demands; ability to access and convey accurate information quickly; ability to work with confidential information, files and records; good safety, attendance and employment records. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor Degree; Experience as a telephone operator or police dispatcher preferred. Mental/Physical Requirements: Selected candidate must have the mental and physical capabilities to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Independently handle minimum 20 pounds. Work is performed in a normal office environment with little exposure to outdoor temperatures or dirt and dust. Working conditions are typically moderately quiet. **Applicants will be required to take a computerized typing test and achieve a typing speed of 35 net words per minute for consideration. Candidates will be contacted to schedule a typing test after their application has been received and reviewed for further consideration. Selected applicant must become member of Teamsters, Chauffeurs and Helpers Local Union and undergo a pre-employment physical and drug screen. Please complete the online application process, upload a resume, complete contact information for three professional references, and any certificates and/or licenses. Please submit all materials at the time of initial application.  Applications will begin being reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Employment at Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check, preemployment physical, and drug screen. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here: https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ . Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 6,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9200120809993_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Bradley University Police Officer - Lateral Transfer",
      "description": "Posted: 2021-08-04\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\n**Applications submitted without a resume and cover letter will not be considered** This position is a member of the Bradley University Department who develops partnerships within and outside the University community and maintains the security and safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors and safeguard the property of the University and its community.  Police Officers are generally assigned to patrol the campus and surrounding areas by car, bike or on foot, making routine checks of campus and residential areas, looking for hazardous, unusual or suspicious conditions requiring police action or assistance.  They assist the injured, elderly and disabled; administer first aid; direct and control campus and surrounding area traffic; investigate suspicious persons and vehicles and secure accident, crime and disaster scenes.  University Officers will interact on a regular basis with federal, state and municipal law enforcement agencies. Police duties involve protection of life and property through the enforcement of laws and ordinances and general police assignments including patrol, preliminary complaint and criminal investigation, traffic control and accident investigation. University Officers identify and apprehend offenders; conduct interviews and interrogations; locate witnesses; seize contraband; conduct warrant checks; perform surveillance; search persons and places; attend court and testify in the trial process and prepare written reports on assigned tasks. Duties may involve an element of personal danger and require University Police Officers to act without direct supervision and exercise independent judgment in emergency situations.  Bradley’s Officers respond to calls and complaints involving fire, automobile accidents, domestic and neighborhood disturbances, assaults, robberies and any other felonies or misdemeanors.  REQUIREMENT FOR LATERAL TRANSFTERS Certification from the Illinois Law Enforcement Training and Standards Board as a certified full time police officer (out-of-state police officers should contact human resources at (309) 677-3223 directly for determination of eligibility) And in good standing in the police department in which the person currently serves or separated from with no adverse employment action And be eligible to be granted a waiver of basic training from the Illinois Law Enforcement Training and Standards Board And must pass medical and background checks And ability to successfully complete a one year probationary period from date of hire and any applicable field training program. WAGE & BENEFIT INFORMATION  Individual pay rate will be from $25.34 to $36.32  per hour depending on prior relevant work experience as determined by the Chief of Police.   Competitive benefits include availability of tuition remission after 1 year of continuous service.  Full benefit offerings provided at https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ MENTAL/PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Selected candidate must have the mental and physical capabilities to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Must be able to walk substantial distances and for prolonged periods of time. Must be able to climb stairs. Must be able to access non-ADA complaint buildings. Many tasks will require the incumbent to be outdoors and exposed to the elements. RECRUITMENT PROCESS Review of Qualifications – Bradley University Police Department will evaluate applications upon receipt. Physical Agility Testing – If required, testing will be arranged by the Bradley University Police Department. Qualified applicants will be notified of dates, times and location for testing. POWER Test and current P.O.W..E.R. standards are included here:  https://www.ptb.illinois.gov/ news/news-important- information/new-power-test- chart/  |   P.O.W.E.R. Test Information Written Examinations – All applicants must successfully pass the written examinations. A large part of a police officer's job involves report writing, reading and interpreting policies and procedures, rules and regulations, state statutes, etc.  These exams are designed to measure abilities in these areas.  Written testing will be arranged by the Human Resource Department. Qualified applications will be notified of dates, times and location for testing. Background Investigation – All qualified candidates are subject to background investigations that include fingerprinting, police records check, and inquiries of neighbors, relatives, employers, etc.   A conviction record may be considered on a case-by-case basis and will not necessarily disqualify a candidate.  Illinois State law precludes appointments as a police officer with any felony conviction or any disqualifying conviction as identified by the Illinois Law Enforcement Training and Standards Board . Personal Interview – A personal interview will be held with selected candidates. Medical Examination – Selected candidates must successfully complete post-offer medical examinations.   APPLICATION PROCEDURE Please complete the online application process and upload a resume, c omplete contact information for three professional references, and any certificates and/or licenses. Please submit all materials at the time of initial application. Applications will begin being reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all the items mentioned in recruitment process. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/  . Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 6,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201843725058_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Online Learning and Distance Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title:  Executive Director of Online Learning and Distance Education Department:  Office of Online and Distance Education Reports To:  Associate Provost for Academic Excellence Appointment: Full-time; 40 hours per week (12-month position) Status: Exempt Bradley University seeks an accomplished, collaborative, and visionary leader to serve as Executive Director of Online Learning and Distance Education. Reporting to the Associate Provost for Academic Excellence, the candidate will provide strategic leadership for the University's online learning ecosystem, serving as the institutional champion for high-quality, student-centered online education.  The Executive Director will lead the development and execution of a university-wide vision for online learning that aligns with Bradley's mission, strategic priorities, and commitment to academic excellence. Working collaboratively with various university units, the Executive Director will cultivate a shared sense of purpose and collective momentum to expand Bradley's reach through innovative online learning opportunities. This is an on-campus position with oversight of a hybrid team. Key Responsibilities Build strong partnerships with deans, department chairs, faculty, and administrative leaders to create broad institutional ownership of online education initiatives.  Lead the strategic expansion of Bradley's portfolio of online and hybrid academic programs, certificates, and professional education offerings.  Guide market-informed program development by collaborating with academic units to identify opportunities aligned with workforce needs and student demand.  Champion excellence in online pedagogy, instructional design, accessibility, quality assurance, and student engagement.  Foster innovation through the thoughtful adoption of emerging educational technologies, including artificial intelligence and digital learning tools, while ensuring they support effective teaching and learning.  Collaborate with Enrollment Management, Marketing and Communications, and academic leadership to strengthen recruitment, retention, and student success for online learners.  Establish metrics and assessment practices to evaluate program quality, learner outcomes, operational effectiveness, and return on investment.  Oversee federal and state compliance for various programs. About the Office The Office of Online and Distance Education partners with faculty and academic units across the University to design, develop, and support high-quality online learning experiences. The office provides expertise in instructional design, educational technology, faculty development, quality standards, project management, and strategic program support while working collaboratively to advance Bradley University's educational mission. Bradley University offers a growing portfolio of undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, certificate, and professional education programs delivered in online and hybrid formats. As learner expectations and workforce needs continue to evolve, the University is committed to expanding flexible, accessible, and academically rigorous educational opportunities that serve traditional students, adult learners, and working professionals. Qualifications Preferred qualifications include: Master's degree required; earned doctorate or other terminal degree preferred.  Significant leadership experience in online learning, digital education, instructional design, academic innovation, or a related area within higher education.  Demonstrated success developing and implementing strategic initiatives that require collaboration across multiple academic and administrative units.  Experience leading organizational change and building consensus among diverse stakeholders.  Knowledge of current and emerging trends in online learning, digital pedagogy, instructional technologies, learning management systems (Canvas), artificial intelligence, accessibility, learning analytics, and student success. Experience supporting faculty in the design and delivery of high-quality online instruction.  Strong communication, project management, and organizational leadership skills.  Proven track record of managing remote or hybrid professionals (e.g., instructional designers, educational technologists, and adjunct staff). Ability to establish clear communication protocols, streamline asynchronous workflows, and foster a strong, collaborative team culture within a distributed work environment. Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201852098656_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Annual Fund Gift Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Annual Fund Gift Officer Department: Advancement Reports To: Executive Director of Donor Engagement Appointment: Full-time, 40 hours per week (12-month position), On Campus Status: Exempt Position Summary The Annual Fund Gift Officer is a front-facing fundraiser responsible for building meaningful relationships with alumni, parents, friends, and Peoria-area community members whose annual giving is generally under $10,000. The officer will qualify, cultivate, solicit, renew, upgrade, and steward a portfolio of donors and prospective donors, with particular emphasis on expanding the Lydia Moss Bradley Society and increasing unrestricted support through the Bradley Fund. This role advances Bradley University’s goals to grow the number of donors, increase alumni participation, strengthen retention and renewal rates, encourage higher levels of annual support, and develop a well-qualified pipeline for major gift portfolios. The officer will engage donors directly through phone and email outreach, virtual and in-person meetings, campus and regional events, and other personalized strategies. The Annual Fund Gift Officer reports to the Executive Director of Donor Engagement and works collaboratively with the Senior Director of the Bradley Fund, the Assistant Director of Annual Giving, and the Assistant Director of Donor Relations. The manager also partners closely with the Vice President for Advancement, Major Gift Officers, Alumni Relations, Advancement Services, and campus colleagues to provide a coordinated, donor-centered experience. Key Responsibilities Portfolio Fundraising and Donor Engagement Build and manage a portfolio of annual giving donors and prospective donors, primarily at the $1,000 to $9,999 level, while cultivating selected donors below $1,000 who demonstrate strong affinity or potential for increased support. Develop and execute individualized strategies to identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, renew, upgrade, and steward donors through phone calls, emails, virtual conversations, in-person meetings, events, and other personal outreach. Conduct meaningful donor contacts and visits and make direct gift solicitations in support of the Bradley Fund and other University priorities. Build relationships with Bradley alumni nationwide and Peoria-area community members, connecting their interests with opportunities to support students and the University. Secure annual commitments, recurring gifts, multi-year pledges when appropriate, and renewed or increased support in alignment with established goals. Lydia Moss Bradley Society Growth Make growth of the Lydia Moss Bradley Society a central focus by identifying, cultivating, and soliciting donors for fully unrestricted annual gifts of $1,000 or more to the Bradley Fund. Develop strategies to retain current Society members, renew lapsed members, upgrade donors into higher recognition levels, and welcome new members through personalized outreach and stewardship. Partner with the Senior Director of the Bradley Fund, Donor Relations, the Society’s volunteer leadership, and university leaders on membership communications, recognition, events, and other engagement opportunities. Annual Giving Initiatives and Collaboration Support the planning and execution of the Bradley Fund’s annual fundraising program, including Day of Giving, targeted appeals, digital campaigns, special initiatives, giving-society efforts, and fiscal year-end outreach. Coordinate closely with the Assistant Director of Annual Giving so that direct donor outreach complements broad-based mail, email, digital, text, and phone strategies. Collaborate with the Associate Director of Donor Relations to ensure assigned donors receive timely, accurate, and meaningful acknowledgment, recognition, impact reporting, and stewardship. Attend and support alumni, donor, campus, and community events, using these opportunities to deepen relationships, identify prospective donors, and advance follow-up strategies. Work with Alumni Relations and campus partners to convert engagement into philanthropy and connect annual giving with the broader Bradley experience. Pipeline Development and Advancement Partnership Identify annual donors with the interest, engagement, and potential to become major gift prospects, and collaborate with the Vice President for Advancement and Major Gift Officers on qualification and transition strategies. Participate in regular portfolio and pipeline reviews, sharing donor intelligence, progress, next steps, and recommended assignments or handoffs. Coordinate outreach with colleagues to avoid duplication, honor existing relationships, and deliver one consistent Bradley donor experience. Prepare donor briefings, contact summaries, solicitation plans, proposals, and follow-up materials as needed. Data Management and Performance Record substantive donor contacts, visits, solicitations, proposals, commitments, interests, and next steps promptly and accurately in Bradley’s CRM, Raiser’s Edge. Maintain accurate portfolio, pipeline, forecast, and pledge information and use data to prioritize outreach and evaluate results. Track and report progress toward annual goals for donor contacts, visits, solicitations, dollars raised, Lydia Moss Bradley Society membership, donor acquisition, retention, renewal, upgrades, and qualified major gift referrals. Use donor data, giving history, engagement information, and available prospect research to develop segmented and personalized outreach strategies. Performance Expectations Meet or exceed annual fundraising, activity, retention, upgrade, membership, and pipeline goals established with the Executive Director of Donor Engagement. Demonstrate disciplined portfolio management, consistent personal outreach, timely follow-through, and a strong commitment to donor service. Contribute to growth in total donors and alumni donors, Bradley Fund revenue, Lydia Moss Bradley Society membership, donor renewal rates, and the number of qualified prospects referred to Major Gift Officers. Maintain the highest standards of confidentiality, integrity, professionalism, collaboration, and donor-centered conduct. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. At least two years of successful fundraising, annual giving, relationship management, sales, business development, alumni engagement, customer development, or closely related experience. Demonstrated ability to build relationships, communicate persuasively, ask for financial commitments, and move donors or clients toward decisions. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and follow-through skills. Ability to manage a portfolio and multiple priorities independently while contributing effectively to a collaborative team. Comfort using data, goals, and performance measures to guide work and assess progress. Proficiency with Google Suite, Microsoft Office and willingness to use a constituent relationship management system consistently and accurately. Ability and willingness to travel regionally and occasionally beyond the region and attend evening and weekend meetings and events. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education advancement, annual giving, nonprofit development, membership development, or a similar relationship-driven environment. Experience managing a donor or client portfolio and successfully renewing or increasing financial commitments. Experience with Raiser’s Edge, GiveCampus, Almabase, or comparable fundraising and engagement platforms. Knowledge of Bradley University, its alumni community, or the Peoria region. Work Environment This position is based at Bradley University in Peoria, Illinois. The role requires regular interaction with donors and prospective donors and includes local, regional and national travel, campus and community events, and occasional evening and weekend responsibilities. Other duties may be assigned in support of Bradley University’s Advancement goals. Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201851352524_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Grounds Maintenance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Grounds Maintenance Department:     Facilities Management Reports to:       Grounds Supervisor Appointment:   Full-time; 40 hours per week, 1st Shift (7:00 am - 3:30 pm) Status:             Non-Exempt Pay Rate:          $22.00 per hour (21.75 to start then $22 per hour after completion of the Teamster's 60-day probationary period). DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES   Provide grounds maintenance support to Facilities Management. Grounds Maintenance includes but is not limited to: preparation, planting, mowing repair, replacement and renovation of ground covers, plants, shrubs, sidewalks, streets and lots; small tree removal and pruning; operation and maintenance of surface and sewer water systems as well as manual and computer based irrigation systems; use, operate, and maintain tools and equipment including tractors, mowers, snowplows, and material handling; operate and use moderate to heavy equipment in efficient safe manner; refuse and garbage maintenance; move and haul property as instructed; some limited brick and concrete work and maintenance of retaining walls; carry out all duties in safe and efficient manner  consistent with University policies and procedures. Varying amount of after hour and special event hours as needed; perform other related duties as assigned.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS   Proven experience with and knowledge of grounds maintenance procedures as stated above; previous experience with manual and power operated equipment including all types of mowers, edgers, chainsaws, etc. related to this position; good comprehensive skills including ability to read and comprehend verbal and written instructions; prior experience operating all related implements and equipment with agility and safety; work as a team and independently; ability to operate forklift; demonstrated good safety, attendance and work record; must have a valid Illinois driver’s license; D.O.T. medium weight truck physical required. Selected candidate must become member of the Teamsters, Chauffeurs and Helpers Local Union.   MENTAL/PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Selected candidate must have the mental and physical capabilities to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation; ability to tolerate constant or extreme noise, independently handle minimum 50 pounds; visual ability to operate equipment effectively and safely; hearing ability to hold conversations through earpiece and in person; speaking ability to effectively communication with other individuals; work environment is primarily outdoor. Ability to tolerate extreme temperatures while working outside is also required. APPLICATION PROCEDURE Please complete the online application process and upload a resume, c omplete contact information for three professional references, and any certificates and/or licenses. Please submit all materials at the time of initial application.  Applications will begin being reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  Employment at Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check, pre-employment physical, and drug screen.  Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/  . Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5.000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201851187718_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "LMS Administrator/Instructional Technologist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title:  LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist Department:  Information Technology Reports To:  Instructional Technology Manager Appointment:  Full-time, 40 hours per week (12-month position), On Campus Status:  Exempt Position Description: The LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist is the principal advisor and point of contact surrounding technologies for learning and their use. They will advise on the selection, design, and implementation of effective instructional technology resources to promote student engagement and success in online, hybrid, and blended courses. This person leads training for instructional technology, and is responsible for providing exceptional customer service as they facilitate, coordinate, and oversee campus-wide use of the LMS and integrated digital tools. The LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist tracks support issues using the campus ticket system, communicates system issues to campus constituents, and evaluates system performance. The LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist is the primary liaison with system vendors and coordinates system upgrades and maintenance with the vendors and the university change management board. Duties include but are not limited to:  System Administration – The LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist works collaboratively with others in IT to proactively manage the learning system and integrated tools used on campus to meet the instructional needs of the university. This requires the individual to understand how the systems work, what data and reporting are available, what changes need to be communicated, and how to effectively test and manage new features, upgrades, and integrations. The primary systems include Canvas, Studio, Bongo, Panopto, Zoom, Respondus, Turnitin, Qualtrics, and Course Evaluations & Surveys. They are licensed SaaS hosted in the cloud by our software vendors. The LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist will be the primary liaison with our vendors to proactively manage these systems. Other campus systems that are managed by others on campus but inter-operate with the above systems include Google Apps for Education, M365, and Microsoft Copilot. Learning Systems Support – This person will serve as second tier support for faculty, staff, and students using the learning systems integrated tools and will be responsible for assisting in the resolution of questions and problems received directly from individuals, tickets received from the Service Desk, and vendor communications. Courteous and respectful interactions with fellow employees and students are to be expected. Good record keeping is necessary to track support issues, system maintenance, upgrades, configurations, and vendor communications. They will need to stay current with emerging educational technologies, including AI applications in teaching and learning, and incorporate relevant innovations into support practices. This person will also support best practices by helping instructors understand ADA requirements for instructional technology. Training and Documentation – The LMS Administrator / Instructional Technologist will advise on the selection, design, and implementation of effective instructional technology resources to promote student engagement and success in online, hybrid, and blended courses. They will train and support faculty through individual consultations, training presentations, and development of instructional materials. This individual will also serve on a team assisting with the creation and administration of Workday training to the campus.  Campus Needs Analysis and System Evaluations – This individual will be responsible for evaluating how well current needs are being met by learning systems. This requires the individual periodically evaluate existing systems usage and end-user satisfaction, analyze findings, and make recommendations for improving systems and services. The LMS administrator will research and maintain currency of knowledge on instructional technologies, industry trends, and recommended practices and participate in or manage new system evaluations and pilots.  Participate on project teams, committees, and attend meetings as necessary. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in instructional technology, instructional design, information technology, education, or similar discipline. Three years of demonstrated success in administering, using, and supporting a learning management system and other instructional technology systems. Excellent customer service and interpersonal skills, preferably in a higher education environment. Effective at developing and delivering training sessions. Excellent written and oral communication skills with individuals possessing varying degrees of technical proficiency. Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions.  Evidence of being a proactive, collaborative problem-solver and team member. Evidence of the ability to take ownership of projects and work independently to achieve expected goals. Proficient in keeping systems records and documenting technical issues and processes. Ability to organize and handle multiple projects simultaneously. Evidence of maintaining confidentiality of private data and upholding information security policies. Preferred Qualifications 5+ years supporting multiple instructional systems, including the LMS Demonstrated success in administering Canvas. Experience in the higher education environment. Experience in gathering systems and support data and generating reports on system use and end-user support. Demonstrated ability to conduct a needs analysis, research and evaluate alternatives, and recommend new systems for adoption. Experience conducting successful pilot tests of potential new systems. Experience managing a system change at an institution. Qualified candidates should submit the following: Current resume and one-page cover letter addressing their skills relevant to the position Complete contact information for three professional references Training materials (link to training videos/materials, and/or upload any training materials that you would like to share) Please submit all materials at the time of initial application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201857222555_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Admission Counselor Department: Enrollment Management Reports To: Director Of Admission Appointment: Full-time, 40 hours per week (12-month position), On Campus Status: Exempt The Division of Enrollment Management invites applications for an energetic and highly motivated admission professional to join our recruitment team. This Admission Counselor position is based on campus in Peoria, Illinois, and will have a primary role in recruiting undergraduate first-year and transfer students to Bradley University.  Position responsibilities include but are not limited to: Represent the University to prospective students and the general public with the highest degree of professionalism through an array of outreach programs and recruitment activities. Manage an individual travel schedule to engage and inform prospective students and their families, as well as develop positive educational partnerships and working relationships with high school counselors. Identify, recruit, and contribute to increasing the population of admitted and enrolled students in designated high schools and regions. Up to six weeks of in-person (and virtual) recruitment travel a year.  Advise prospective students and family members about admission criteria, the financial assistance process and other critical factors in the college decision process. Participate in a variety of projects and events related to student recruitment both on and off campus. Review and assess applications and make university admission and scholarship recommendations. Analyze current and historical admissions results and trends within the geographic territory and develop and implement strategies to surpass enrollment goals. Utilize CRM Slate to maintain updated records and communication with students, parents and school counselors. Education & Experience   Bachelor's degree (B.A.) from a four-year college or university Candidates must possess the following skills and abilities : Strong interpersonal and communication skills are required Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects; flexible and comfortable in a fast-paced environment, with excellent follow through. Ability to work independently as well as within a team environment.  Entrepreneurial spirit, positive attitude, and energy to implement new strategies and meet ambitious goals. Strong organization skills, with keen attention to detail. Willingness to travel and work evenings and weekends. Preference will be given to candidates with college admission experience.  Due to the nature of this position, evening and weekend work can be expected throughout the year, especially during the fall and spring. Candidates should also be prepared to travel overnight based upon the geographic territory assigned and must possess a valid US driver’s license. While the majority of the work is done sitting or standing, the ability to lift boxes weighing up to 40 pounds is also necessary. Candidates may need to access Non-ADA compliant buildings. Candidates must demonstrate strong oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills; the ability to work independently and within a team environment; possess strong analytical and independent decision making ability; as well as the ability to work with a diverse population. Working knowledge of MS Office applications is required. Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  To ensure full consideration, application materials should be received by November 20, 2026. The ideal start date for this position is January 4, 2027. While the review of applications will begin immediately, applications will be accepted until positions are filled.  Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201857209575_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Graphic Designer Department: Marketing Reports To: Brand Manager & Lead Designer Appointment: Full-time, 40 hours per week (12-month position), On Campus Status: Exempt Bradley University is seeking a creative, collaborative, and detail-oriented Graphic Designer to join the University’s Marketing and Communications team. The Graphic Designer will play an important role in bringing the Bradley brand to life through compelling visual storytelling across print, digital, environmental, and other marketing channels. Working within Bradley’s integrated Marketing and Communications operation, this position will develop creative solutions that support University priorities, with particular emphasis on student recruitment and enrollment, institutional reputation, academic programs, advancement, and campus engagement. The ideal candidate is a versatile designer who combines strong creative instincts with an understanding of strategic marketing. This individual should be comfortable managing multiple projects simultaneously, collaborating with a variety of campus partners, and translating complex ideas into engaging, audience-focused visual communications. This position reports to the Brand Manager and Lead Designer and is based on Bradley University’s campus in Peoria, Illinois. Primary Responsibilities Creative Design and Brand Execution Design high-quality visual materials that support Bradley University’s marketing, communications, recruitment, and institutional priorities. Create materials across a wide range of formats, including digital advertising, social media graphics, email campaigns, publications, brochures, postcards, event materials, presentations, signage, environmental graphics, and other collateral. Translate marketing strategies, creative briefs, and institutional priorities into compelling visual concepts and finished creative products. Apply Bradley University's visual identity consistently while finding creative opportunities to strengthen and evolve the University's visual storytelling. Serve as a steward of Bradley's brand standards and help campus partners understand and effectively apply the University's visual identity. Develop templates, design systems, and other resources that create consistency and efficiency across University communications. Digital and Integrated Marketing Design digital assets optimized for websites, email, social media, digital advertising, and other online platforms. Work collaboratively with web, content, social media, video, photography, and marketing colleagues to develop cohesive integrated campaigns. Create adaptable creative concepts that can be effectively executed across multiple platforms, formats, and audience segments. Maintain awareness of emerging design practices, digital marketing trends, and evolving audience expectations. Ensure designs meet appropriate accessibility standards and follow best practices for digital and print communications. Collaboration and Project Management Work with campus partners to understand project goals, audiences, messaging, timelines, and desired outcomes. Participate in brainstorming, campaign development, creative reviews, and other collaborative planning processes. Manage multiple projects and deadlines while maintaining a high level of quality and attention to detail. Communicate effectively with internal clients regarding project scope, timelines, revisions, and deliverables. Prepare production-ready files and coordinate as needed with printers, vendors, photographers, and other external partners. Maintain organized project files, templates, design assets, and brand resources. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's marketing and communications priorities. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in graphic design, visual communication, communication design, marketing, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Demonstrated professional experience in graphic design, visual communication, or a related creative role. Strong portfolio demonstrating creativity, typography, layout, visual hierarchy, brand application, and design across multiple media. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud, particularly Adobe InDesign, Illustrator, and Photoshop. Demonstrated ability to design for both print and digital environments. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines. Excellent attention to detail. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to receive feedback, collaborate effectively, and translate strategic direction into creative solutions. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education, agency, nonprofit, or another complex organization with multiple audiences and stakeholders. Experience developing creative for student recruitment, consumer marketing, or integrated marketing campaigns. Experience designing for paid digital advertising, social media, email marketing, and web environments. Experience working within established brand standards and contributing to the development or evolution of a visual identity. Familiarity with digital accessibility and inclusive design practices. Experience with motion graphics, animation, video graphics, photography, or basic video editing is a plus. Familiarity with tools such as Canva, Figma, or similar collaborative design platforms is a plus. Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  To ensure full consideration, application materials should be received by November 20, 2026. The ideal start date for this position is January 4, 2027. While the review of applications will begin immediately, applications will be accepted until positions are filled.  Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
