    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201857616048_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Instructor in Residence, Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nThe Department of Biology at Bradley University invites applications for an Instructor in Residence for Spring 2027. This one semester, non-renewable position will contribute to the undergraduate curriculum, with primary teaching responsibilities in introductory molecular biology lecture (non-majors) and laboratory courses (first-year majors). These courses will support students across the Department of Biology (Biology, Biomedical Sciences, and Environmental Sciences), the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry (Chemistry, Biochemistry, and Medical Laboratory Science), and allied health programs, including Nursing, Kinesiology, and Health Sciences. The instructor-level appointment will involve a teaching load of 12 contact hours for the semester, with no expectations for research activity or additional service responsibilities. We seek a dedicated educator committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching and to supporting a diverse student population in a liberal arts and sciences environment. The successful candidate will employ active learning strategies, foster inclusive and engaging classroom experiences, and provide personalized attention to students with varied backgrounds, experiences, and learning needs. Candidates must possess a MS in Biology or a related field, with a strong background in molecular biology coursework or significant experience in molecular biology. Prior teaching experience is preferred. Application Materials  Qualified applicants should submit the following materials: A letter of application A curriculum vitae Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required prior to the issuance of a final offer letter. A statement of teaching philosophy and interests Diversity statement that includes your demonstrated commitment to, past evidence of, and future plans for creating equitable opportunities for underrepresented students. Contact information for three references. References will be contacted following an initial screening. Applicants should also describe their strategies for engaging and supporting a diverse student population through teaching. This information may be included in the letter of application or submitted as a separate diversity statement. Please submit all materials at the time of initial application . Completed applications will be reviewed beginning immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Employment at Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
