      "title": "Director of the Mathematics Success Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nAcademic Success Center and Academic Affairs - Tenure Track Lecturer and Director of Math Success Center Applications are invited for a tenure track lecturer and Director of the Mathematics Success Center position beginning May 2027. Duties include serving as the coordinator of the mathematics portion of Bradley University's Academic Success Center, teaching foundational mathematics courses (face-to-face and online), data analysis, and providing collaborative support in math pedagogy for math faculty and all faculty who teach courses that emphasize quantitative reasoning. Director responsibilities include the following: 1. Work directly with students struggling with prerequisite skills for foundational mathematics courses by developing individualized plans for success  2. Work with advisors, faculty, and staff on proactive outreach to struggling students  3. Collaborate with the Mathematics Department, College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, Admissions, and the Provost’s Office to increase math success and student retention university wide  4. Develop and implement professional development opportunities focused on math success and student retention for faculty and staff   5. Develop math success programs and math tutor training aligned with best practices   6. Evaluate data on effectiveness of Center programs, student success in mathematics courses, retention, and other metrics  7. Provide actionable recommendations towards meeting Center goals aligned with the University Strategic Plan  8. Promote and develop online/hybrid Center resources as appropriate  9. Oversee the year-round operations of the Center including: on-boarding first-year and transfer students, budgeting, integration of third-party platforms (e.g. Navigate360, ALEKS),  website content, and collaboration with other University offices   10. Coordinate math preparation courses, train qualified faculty, and teach as necessary  11. Other duties as needed and assigned  All candidates must have at least a Master’s in mathematics education, mathematics, or an equivalent field and have educational experience in math pedagogy.  Evidence of exceptional teaching at the high school level or teaching developmental math at the college level is required.  Experience teaching at the high school level and working in math success at the college level is preferred. Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching, have experience with the ALEKS software package, and who are knowledgeable about Illinois Teacher Licensure requirements.    TO APPLY: Qualified candidates should submit a letter of application, CV, a copy of graduate and undergraduate transcripts, a statement of teaching philosophy, and a list of three references who can address teaching qualifications. Please include a description of strategies for engaging a diverse student population, either in the letter of application, in the statement of teaching philosophy, or as a separate statement. Please upload all documents at the time of initial application .  Review of applications will begin November 9th and continue until the position is filled.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here: www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits . Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
