    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201839236768_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Studio Art",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nBradley University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Studio Art in the Department of Art and Design, to begin Fall of 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching, an active and evolving creative practice, and the ability to provide meaningful service to the department, college, and university. The position supports the university’s mission of integrating teaching excellence, creative inquiry, and student mentorship. Responsibilities will include, but are not limited to :   - Teach a range of undergraduate courses at the introductory and advanced levels in one or more disciplines (such as drawing, printmaking, ceramics, photography, new media, installation art, or sculpture)  - Develop and deliver coursework that emphasizes both traditional and contemporary art practices  - The ability to teach 3D foundations classes is desirable.  - Maintain an active program of creative research appropriate for tenure and promotion  - Advise and mentor undergraduate students, including academic advising and portfolio development  - Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and program planning  - Contribute to departmental, college, and university service, including committees and outreach  - Assist with recruitment, retention, and student exhibitions Qualifications : Required:  - Ability & willingness to teach foundational courses  - MFA in an appropriate studio art discipline   - Evidence of effective undergraduate teaching or clear potential for teaching excellence  - Demonstrated record or strong potential for creative scholarship appropriate to a tenure-track appointment  - Commitment to inclusive, student-centered pedagogy  - Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Working Conditions :  - Hands-on work in active studio environments with potential exposure to dust, chemicals, and power tools. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, current vita, and contact information for three professional references. Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  The deadline to submit applications is December 1, 2026. Employment at Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201839227509_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nThe Management and Leadership Department of Bradley University’s AACSB accredited Foster College of Business invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management position effective Fall 2027. We seek applicants with teaching and research interests related to strategic management. Teaching responsibilities are primarily in strategic management, including the undergraduate senior business capstone, but may also include principles of management, organizational theory, organizational effectiveness, or other areas of management as needed. The position may involve teaching both in-person and online undergraduate and graduate courses. Commitment to and evidence of outstanding teaching, strong publication potential, and a focused research agenda are required. Faculty are expected to maintain a high level of professional activity through scholarly research and service. Competitive candidates will have a doctorate in management or closely related field from an AACSB-accredited school; ABDs will be considered.  The Foster College of Business creates ideas that advance business thought and practice, provides experiential learning that develops leaders who will enrich the world, and serves as a valued partner for business and society. Located in the newly constructed 200,000 square foot Business and Engineering Convergence Center, the Foster College offers unique opportunities for collaboration and convergence between Bradley’s business and engineering colleges. Accredited by the AACSB, the Foster College of Business offers exceptional teaching, small class sizes, and requires all students to participate in experiential learning. Visit http://www.bradley.edu/academics/colleges/fcba/ to learn more about the college. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, current vita, teaching evaluations (if available) or other documentation of teaching potential, and contact information for three professional references. Please submit all materials at the initial time of application. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Employment at Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201814389179_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Construction",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nThe Department of Civil Engineering and Construction at Bradley University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor or Lecturer level in Construction. This is an on-campus faculty position with a primary focus on teaching and developing undergraduate and graduate courses, supervising students, engaging in service, and/or participating in scholarly activities. We are a committed, student-centered program in Central Illinois that prioritizes accessible undergraduate education, effective pedagogy, and an inclusive learning environment. The application review will start immediately and continue until the position is filled.  Applicants should have earned a PhD in Architecture, Construction Management, or other appropriate field. The minimum requirements are a Master’s degree in architecture or construction management and relevant industry or teaching experience. For the tenure-track assistant professor position, preference will be given to candidates with a PhD and significant industry and teaching experience. Individuals with a Master’s degree and relevant industry or teaching experience in Construction Management will be considered for the tenure-track Lecturer position, depending on applicant qualifications. For the Lecturer position, scholarly activities are encouraged but not necessarily required. Preference will be given to candidates whose motivations and skill sets align with genuine care for students and their success, continuous improvement, and service to their profession and Bradley University. The successful applicant will have a broad background in construction management or architecture, including estimating, scheduling, project management, safety, surveying, sustainability, and proficiency in computer software applications such as CADD, as well as the ability to teach other civil engineering or construction courses as needed. Salary and rank are commensurate with qualifications. TO APPLY: Interested applicants must submit (1) a letter of interest addressing the qualifications for the position, (2) a complete resume/vita, (3) contact information for at least three professional references, (4) a statement of teaching interests with a list of courses that the applicant can teach, (5) undergraduate and graduate transcripts (copies are sufficient), and (6) statement of commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application. The Department of Civil Engineering and Construction has a strong tradition of excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service to society and the profession. CEC faculty are active researchers, have strong ties to major industrial partners, and are active in professional organizations such as ACCE, ACI, AISC, ASC, ASCE, MCAA, and others. The department has 10 full-time faculty members and approximately 200 students.  Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here: www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits . Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201827526331_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nApplications are invited for a tenure-track assistant/associate professor position in the Accounting Department at Bradley University starting January 2027 or August 2027. The successful candidate is expected to teach, conduct scholarly research, mentor students, and contribute service to the university and community. We seek applicants with teaching and research interests related to financial accounting, although other subdisciplines within accounting will be considered. The successful candidate should also be willing to offer courses in financial or managerial principles. The position may involve teaching both in person and online courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Commitment to and evidence of outstanding teaching, strong publication potential, and a focused research agenda are required. Faculty are expected to maintain a high level of scholarly research and service. The Foster College of Business is proud to be one of only 189 schools that are AACSB accredited in both business and accounting. The college is co-located with the Caterpillar College of Engineering and Technology in a $100 million state-of-the-art facility, the Business and Engineering Convergence Center, which provides an exceptional collaborative teaching and learning environment. Bradley University ranked #183 overall nationally in the 2025 U.S. News and World Report with a top 40 undergraduate engineering program. Bradley offers more than 185 undergraduate and graduate academic programs in business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. We are committed to cultivating an inclusive and welcoming environment at Bradley for a diverse group of students, faculty, and staff. The Accounting Department is one of five departments in the Foster College of Business, which serves approximately 600 undergraduate business students through 17 programs of study and offers several graduate programs. Bradley's Accounting program delivers top-tier results to its students, with student CPA Exam pass rates consistently ranking among Illinois's best. Qualifications: A Ph.D. or terminal degree (e.g., JD/LLM) in Accounting or closely related field is required, although those with ABD status with expected degree completion prior to start date will be considered. A degree from an AASCB-accredited institution and professional credential is preferred. Applicants must have an understanding of, and a commitment to, creating an inclusive environment, and the ability to work with a diverse group of students, faculty, and staff. Strong preference will be given to candidates with a professional certification and work experience in the profession. Required Application Materials: A complete online application must be received by electronic submission to be considered, to include: Cover letter describing qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research activity and plan Contact information (name, telephone number, and email address) for 3 professional references Please submit all materials at the time of initial application. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here: www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits . Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
