    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201800555728_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Affiliate Instructor, Communication (COM 103 - Basic Course)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-12\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nThe Department of Communication, within the Slane College of Communications and Fine Arts at Bradley University, seeks candidates committed to innovative teaching and meaningful service in the area of public speaking, oral communication, and foundational communication skills instruction. We seek to attract a faculty who value working with a diverse student body and who are dedicated to helping students develop confidence, critical thinking, and ethical communication practices. Bradley University’s Oral Communication Process Program (COM103) is nationally recognized, designated as a National Communication Association (NCA) Program of Excellence, reflecting a strong commitment to excellence in communication education, student success, and nationally recognized teaching practices. COM 103 serves as the foundational communication course for students across the university and plays a central role in advancing these standards of excellence.   Salary Salary commensurate with education and experience. Job Summary/Basic Function Required: Experience teaching public speaking, oral communication, interpersonal communication, or related communication coursework with a demonstrated commitment to student-centered instruction and high-impact teaching practices. The successful candidate will teach COM 103: Oral Communication Process , Bradley University’s foundational basic course in communication. COM 103 emphasizes public speaking, audience analysis, organization and delivery of speeches, informative and persuasive speaking, listening, critical thinking, and ethical communication practices. The number of sections will be determined by need each semester. This is an in-person course , offered each Fall and Spring semester. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to: Teach foundational public speaking and presentation skills to students from a wide range of majors and academic backgrounds  Foster inclusive classroom environments that support communication confidence and student engagement  Provide effective feedback on speech preparation, delivery, and presentation performance  Support students in developing oral communication competencies aligned with university-wide learning outcomes  Utilize instructional technologies and active learning strategies to enhance student success  Also desirable: Experience teaching the basic communication course at the college level  Familiarity with communication assessment practices and speech evaluation  Experience in argumentation, civic discourse, or communication across the curriculum  Ability to contribute to departmental initiatives supporting speech education and student success  Required Education Master’s degree in Communication, Speech Communication, Communication Studies, Rhetoric, or a closely related field required.  Documents Needed to Apply To successfully apply, applicants must include: Curriculum vitae  Cover letter describing teaching philosophy and interest in the position  Please upload all documents at the time of initial application. Review of applications will continue until the position(s) is filled. Applications to this posting are maintained as a pool for consideration of appointments that may become available. For additional information about the Slane College of Communication and Fine Arts and the Department of Communication visit: www.bradley.edu/academic/colleges/cfa/ www.bradley.edu/academic/departments/communication/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, prestigious, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering 5,400 undergraduate and graduate students the opportunities, choices, and resources of a larger university and the personal attention and exceptional learning experience of a smaller university. Bradley offers a comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs in business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. The University is located on an 85-acre campus in Peoria, the largest metropolitan area in Central Illinois. Visit www.bradley.edu for additional information about the University. Bradley University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. The administration, faculty, and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
